# ARCHITECTURE RULES

## MODULAR MONOLITH

The MVP uses a modular monolith.

Do not create microservices.

Do not create unnecessary abstraction layers.

Organize code by domain.

Example:

lib/
  boards/
  faces/
  occupancy/
  compliance/
  enquiries/
  field/
  marketplace/

Each domain may contain:

service.ts
queries.ts
mutations.ts
validation.ts
types.ts
utils.ts

Do not force every domain to contain every file.

---

# UI VS BUSINESS LOGIC

React components are responsible for:

- rendering
- user interaction
- local UI state

Business logic belongs in:

- server actions
- domain services
- database functions
- validated server-side operations

Do not put complex database workflows inside components.

---

# SERVER VS CLIENT

Prefer Server Components.

Use Client Components only when needed for:

- interaction
- browser APIs
- forms requiring client interaction
- maps
- QR scanning
- geolocation
- offline functionality

Do not mark entire pages "use client" unnecessarily.

This project uses Next.js 16. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using APIs that may have changed.

---

# DATA ACCESS

Do not fetch the same data repeatedly from multiple components.

Create reusable typed data access functions.

Avoid:

component A → Supabase
component B → Supabase
component C → Supabase

when one server-side query can provide the required page data.

Use existing clients:

- `lib/supabase/server.ts` — Server Components, Server Actions, Route Handlers
- `lib/supabase/client.ts` — browser only
- `lib/supabase/admin.ts` — service role, server-only (`import "server-only"`)
- `lib/supabase/proxy.ts` — session refresh / route gating

Never import the admin client from Client Components.

---

# ERROR HANDLING

Never expose raw database errors.

Translate technical errors into useful user-facing messages.

Example:

BAD:

duplicate key value violates exclusion constraint

GOOD:

"This face already has a reservation during the selected dates."

Log technical details server-side where appropriate.

---

# TYPES

Avoid:

any

as unknown as X

unless absolutely necessary and documented.

Database types should be generated from Supabase schema where practical.

Never duplicate database types manually if generated types can be used.
